  "prefLabel": "Ph 704.03 Patient Counseling",
  "priorExpiration": "2013-03-26",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ph 704.03 Patient Counseling.\n\n(a) Patient counseling shall be appropriate based on the pharmacist’s professional and clinical judgement according to current standards of practice.\n\n(b) A pharmacist shall not be required to counsel a patient or agent when the patient or agent refuses such consultation. However, failure to document the patient's refusal of counseling shall imply that counseling was provided.\n\nSource. #5552 INTERIM eff 1-8-93, EXPIRES 5-8-93; ss by #5622, eff 5-8-93; ss by #6181-B, eff 2-5-96, EXPIRED: 2-5-04\n\nNew. #8316, eff 3-26-05, EXPIRED: 3-26-13\n\nNew. #10903, eff 8-5-15; ss by #13398, eff 6-22-22 (formerly Ph 706.03) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ph 700)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ph100-2600.html"
